== an sh shebang rejects the three bash conditions:
TMPDIR/sh-script:2:20: error: Builtin `trap`: ERR: invalid signal specification.
     2 |  trap "echo action" ERR
       |                     ^~~
note: List the signal names with `trap -l`.
err-rc=1
TMPDIR/sh-script:4:20: error: Builtin `trap`: RETURN: invalid signal specification.
     4 |  trap "echo action" RETURN
       |                     ^~~~~~
note: List the signal names with `trap -l`.
return-rc=1
TMPDIR/sh-script:6:20: error: Builtin `trap`: DEBUG: invalid signal specification.
     6 |  trap "echo action" DEBUG
       |                     ^~~~~
note: List the signal names with `trap -l`.
debug-rc=1
body
rc=0
== a bash shebang accepts all three:
err-rc=0
return-rc=0
action
debug-rc=0
action
